<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<properties>
    <!-- No default server, deliberately.

         From 1.2.0 through 1.3.0 this shipped as one developer's personal
         free-tier ngrok tunnel, named in the 1.3.1 changelog entry and
         deliberately not repeated in a file that ships. Every store install
         therefore found a non-empty ServerUrl,
         skipped the setup screen entirely, POSTed /api/pair at a host that was
         usually offline, and rendered "Pairing failed" forever. It was reported
         from a Forerunner 55 on 2026-09-02 and it affected every user on every
         device; nobody who installed from the store could ever pair.

         Worse when the tunnel was up: a stranger's watch minted a pairing code
         against the developer's own health server, one approval click away from
         handing out a bearer token to somebody else's Garmin data.

         The earlier justification for a baked default was that sideloaded
         installs get no settings screen. That is true, and it is a developer
         problem rather than a user one: build with monkey-dev.jungle to
         sideload, which layers resources-dev over this file. See ciq/README.md.

         An empty value makes getServerUrl() return null, which is what routes a
         fresh install to the "Setup required" screen, the honest answer to a
         watch that has no server to talk to yet. -->
    <property id="ServerUrl" type="string"></property>
</properties>
